=== reactor ===
The reactor freezes the sponsored clip on her face. “Can we stop?” The edit cuts before she finishes. The headline calls it a breakup tease.
-> venue

=== studio ===
In the uncut clip she finishes the sentence. “I still want to see you. I just don't want them to see us.”
After the cameras leave, she goes back to the project she has been building. An act whose lore fits the work is ready to lead it. For the first time, she sees a way to keep the project going on her own terms.
-> venue

=== venue ===
Her partner takes the stage with another artist. A camera swings toward the wings, waiting for her reaction. She walks out of frame and keeps going.
She takes the deal with the act that can lead her project. It gives the work a future outside the sponsored romance.
* [See what happens next]
    -> license_request

=== license_request ===
The studio footage runs past the usual cut. She is at the console, calling for another take. She is the overlooked fifth artist. She wrote the song, financed the session and kept the master under the signed agreement.
A producer asks to license that recording for her former partner's next production. She opens the request and sees his name. The decision is hers.
Cut to black.
-> END
